skill: Logical Reasoning

@ Number Series | B
What comes next in the series 2, 4, 6, 8, ?
= 10
- 9
- 12
- 14
? The series increases by 2 each time.

@ Number Series | B
What comes next in the series 3, 6, 12, 24, ?
= 48
- 36
- 30
- 60
? Each number is double the previous one.

@ Number Series | I
What comes next in the series 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, ?
= 36
- 30
- 49
- 35
? These are square numbers: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 squared, so the next is 6 squared = 36.

@ Number Series | I
What comes next in the series 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, ?
= 13
- 12
- 14
- 15
? These are consecutive prime numbers, and the next prime after 11 is 13.

@ Number Series | I
What comes next in the series 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, ?
= 13
- 11
- 12
- 16
? Each term is the sum of the previous two (Fibonacci): 5 + 8 = 13.

@ Number Series | A
What comes next in the series 2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?
= 42
- 40
- 36
- 44
? The differences are 4, 6, 8, 10, so the next difference is 12 and 30 + 12 = 42.

@ Number Series | A
What comes next in the series 1, 2, 6, 24, 120, ?
= 720
- 240
- 600
- 480
? Each term is multiplied by 2, 3, 4, 5 and then 6: 120 x 6 = 720.

@ Coding-Decoding | B
If CAT is coded as DBU by moving each letter one step forward, how is DOG coded?
= EPH
- CNF
- DPH
- EOH
? Each letter moves one place forward: D to E, O to P, G to H.

@ Coding-Decoding | B
If A = 1, B = 2, C = 3 and so on, what is the sum of the letter values of ACE?
= 9
- 8
- 10
- 15
? A = 1, C = 3, E = 5, and 1 + 3 + 5 = 9.

@ Coding-Decoding | I
If PENCIL is coded as QFODJM, how is BOOK coded?
= CPPL
- CPOL
- APPL
- BPPL
? Each letter moves one step forward: B to C, O to P, O to P, K to L.

@ Coding-Decoding | I
If MONDAY is written as NPOEBZ, how is FRIDAY written in the same code?
= GSJEBZ
- GSJEBY
- ESHCZX
- GRJEBZ
? Each letter moves one step forward: F to G, R to S, I to J, D to E, A to B, Y to Z.

@ Coding-Decoding | I
If A = 1, B = 2 and so on, what is the sum of the values of the letters in BAD?
= 7
- 6
- 8
- 9
? B = 2, A = 1, D = 4, and the sum is 7.

@ Coding-Decoding | A
In a certain code, + means - and - means +. What is the value of 15 + 5 - 3?
= 13
- 17
- 23
- 7
? With the symbols swapped, the expression is 15 - 5 + 3 = 13.

@ Blood Relations | B
A is the brother of B. B is the mother of C. How is A related to C?
= Maternal uncle
- Father
- Paternal uncle
- Grandfather
? A is the brother of C's mother, so A is C's maternal uncle.

@ Blood Relations | I
Pointing to a man, Rita says, "He is the son of my mother's only son." How is the man related to Rita?
= Nephew
- Brother
- Son
- Cousin
? Rita's mother's only son is Rita's brother, so the man is her brother's son, which is her nephew.

@ Blood Relations | I
X is the father of Y. Y is the sister of Z. Z is the son of W. How is W related to X?
= Wife
- Sister
- Mother
- Daughter
? Y and Z are siblings, so W is a parent of Y. X is Y's father, so W is X's wife.

@ Blood Relations | I
Introducing a woman, Arun says, "Her mother is the only daughter of my mother." How is the woman related to Arun?
= Niece
- Sister
- Daughter
- Cousin
? The only daughter of Arun's mother is Arun's sister, so the woman is the daughter of his sister: his niece.

@ Blood Relations | B
A is the mother of B. B is the sister of C. D is the father of C. How is D related to B?
= Father
- Brother
- Uncle
- Grandfather
? B and C are siblings, so D is the father of both.

@ Direction Sense | B
A man walks 5 km north and then 5 km south. How far is he from the starting point?
= 0 km
- 5 km
- 10 km
- 2.5 km
? The two movements cancel out.

@ Direction Sense | I
A man walks 3 km east and then 4 km north. What is his straight-line distance from the start?
= 5 km
- 7 km
- 6 km
- 1 km
? The two legs form a right triangle, and sqrt(3^2 + 4^2) = 5.

@ Direction Sense | I
A person faces east and turns right twice. Which direction does he face now?
= West
- North
- South
- East
? Facing east, the first right turn gives south and the second gives west.

@ Direction Sense | I
A man faces south and turns 90 degrees anticlockwise. Which direction does he face now?
= East
- West
- North
- South-West
? When facing south, turning anticlockwise (to the left) points to the east.

@ Direction Sense | A
A walks 10 m east, turns left and walks 5 m, then turns left again and walks 10 m. How far and in which direction is he from the start?
= 5 m north
- 5 m south
- 10 m west
- 15 m north
? East 10 then north 5 then west 10 brings him back to the starting column, 5 m north of the start.

@ Syllogisms | B
All cats are animals. All animals are living beings. Conclusion: All cats are living beings.
= Definitely follows
- Does not follow
- Only some cats are living beings
- Cannot be determined
? Both premises chain together, so every cat is a living being.

@ Syllogisms | I
Some pens are books. All books are tables. Conclusion: Some pens are tables.
= Definitely follows
- Does not follow
- All pens are tables
- No pen is a table
? The pens that are books are also tables, so some pens are tables.

@ Syllogisms | I
All A are B. Some B are C. Conclusion: Some A are C.
= Does not necessarily follow
- Definitely follows
- No A is C
- All A are C
? The B that are C might not be the B that are A, so the conclusion is not guaranteed.

@ Syllogisms | I
No dog is a cat. Some cats are pets. Conclusion: Some pets are not dogs.
= Definitely follows
- Does not follow
- All pets are dogs
- No pet is a cat
? The pets that are cats cannot be dogs, so some pets are not dogs.

@ Syllogisms | A
All roses are flowers. Some flowers fade quickly. Conclusions: I. Some roses fade quickly. II. Some flowers are roses. Which follows?
= Only conclusion II follows
- Only conclusion I follows
- Both follow
- Neither follows
? Some flowers are roses follows from all roses being flowers. The fading flowers need not be roses.

@ Ordering and Ranking | B
In a row of 10 people, Ravi is 4th from the left. What is his position from the right?
= 7th
- 6th
- 5th
- 4th
? Position from the right = 10 - 4 + 1 = 7.

@ Ordering and Ranking | I
Asha is 7th from the front and 9th from the back in a queue. How many people are in the queue?
= 15
- 16
- 17
- 14
? Total = 7 + 9 - 1 = 15.

@ Ordering and Ranking | I
Four people A, B, C and D sit in a row. D is at the left end, A is to the left of B, and C is to the right of B. Who is third from the left?
= B
- A
- C
- D
? The order from the left is D, A, B, C, so B is third.

@ Ordering and Ranking | I
A is taller than B, B is taller than C, D is taller than A, and E is shorter than C. Who is the shortest?
= E
- C
- B
- D
? The order from tallest to shortest is D, A, B, C, E.

@ Ordering and Ranking | A
Rani ranks 12th from the top and 28th from the bottom in a class. How many students are in the class?
= 39
- 40
- 38
- 41
? Total = 12 + 28 - 1 = 39.

@ Analogies and Odd One Out | B
Hand : Glove :: Foot : ?
= Sock
- Shoe lace
- Knee
- Toe
? A glove is worn on the hand and a sock is worn on the foot.

@ Analogies and Odd One Out | B
Which one is the odd one out: Apple, Banana, Carrot, Mango?
= Carrot
- Apple
- Banana
- Mango
? Carrot is a vegetable while the others are fruits.

@ Analogies and Odd One Out | I
Doctor : Hospital :: Teacher : ?
= School
- Book
- Student
- Exam
? A doctor works in a hospital and a teacher works in a school.

@ Analogies and Odd One Out | I
Pen : Write :: Knife : ?
= Cut
- Sharp
- Steel
- Kitchen
? The relationship is a tool and its function.

@ Analogies and Odd One Out | I
Which number is the odd one out: 8, 27, 64, 100, 125?
= 100
- 8
- 64
- 125
? The others are perfect cubes: 2^3, 3^3, 4^3 and 5^3.

@ Analogies and Odd One Out | A
Which one is the odd one out: Python, Java, Linux, C++?
= Linux
- Python
- Java
- C++
? Linux is an operating system while the others are programming languages.

@ Calendar and Clock | B
Today is Monday. What day will it be after 10 days?
= Thursday
- Wednesday
- Friday
- Sunday
? 10 days is 1 week and 3 days, so Monday plus 3 days is Thursday.

@ Calendar and Clock | I
5 March 2024 is a Tuesday. What day is 5 April 2024?
= Friday
- Thursday
- Saturday
- Wednesday
? March has 31 days, which is 4 weeks and 3 days, so Tuesday plus 3 days is Friday.

@ Calendar and Clock | I
How many times do the hands of a clock overlap in 12 hours?
= 11
- 12
- 10
- 24
? The hands overlap 11 times in 12 hours, because the 12 o'clock overlap at the end coincides with the start of the next cycle.

@ Calendar and Clock | I
What is the angle between the hour hand and the minute hand at 3:00?
= 90 degrees
- 60 degrees
- 120 degrees
- 180 degrees
? Each hour mark is 30 degrees apart, and 3 hours is 90 degrees.

@ Calendar and Clock | A
What is the angle between the hands of a clock at 3:15?
= 7.5 degrees
- 0 degrees
- 15 degrees
- 22.5 degrees
? The hour hand is at 3 x 30 + 15 x 0.5 = 97.5 degrees and the minute hand is at 90 degrees, so the angle is 7.5 degrees.

@ Puzzles and Reasoning | A
A father is 4 times as old as his son. After 6 years he will be 3 times as old as his son. What is the son's present age?
= 12 years
- 6 years
- 10 years
- 15 years
? Let the son be x. Then 4x + 6 = 3(x + 6), so x = 12.

@ Puzzles and Reasoning | I
The sum of two numbers is 40 and their difference is 10. What is the larger number?
= 25
- 30
- 20
- 15
? The numbers are (40 + 10) / 2 = 25 and (40 - 10) / 2 = 15.

@ Puzzles and Reasoning | B
If 6 pencils cost 18 rupees, how much do 15 pencils cost?
= 45 rupees
- 30 rupees
- 40 rupees
- 54 rupees
? One pencil costs 3 rupees, so 15 pencils cost 45 rupees.

@ Puzzles and Reasoning | I
All students who study regularly pass the exam. Ravi studies regularly. What can be concluded?
= Ravi passes the exam
- Ravi may fail
- Ravi is the topper
- Nothing can be concluded
? The rule applies to everyone who studies regularly, so Ravi passes.

@ Puzzles and Reasoning | A
Which statement is the contrapositive of "If it rains, the ground is wet"?
= If the ground is not wet, it did not rain
- If the ground is wet, it rained
- If it does not rain, the ground is not wet
- If the ground is wet, it did not rain
? The contrapositive swaps and negates both parts, and it is always logically equivalent to the original statement.

@ Number Series | I
In a code, 2 becomes 4, 3 becomes 9, 4 becomes 16. What does 7 become?
= 49
- 14
- 21
- 28
? Each number is squared, so 7 becomes 49.

@ Number Series | I
Which letter completes the series A, C, E, G, ?
= I
- H
- J
- K
? The letters skip one letter each time.

@ Number Series | I
What comes next in the series AZ, BY, CX, ?
= DW
- DV
- EW
- CW
? The first letter moves forward and the second moves backward each time.
